{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met the responsibility chain: the doctor recognized high-risk odontogenic/maxillofacial infection rather than ordinary “上火,” directed same-day emergency/oral-maxillofacial evaluation with CT/labs, repeatedly operationalized red flags, avoided self-medication, and closed with discharge medication/wound-care/return precautions confirmed by family. No serious or minor responsibility-chain defect is evident. Multiple high-order points were actively completed, including explaining source control to reduce fear of drainage, avoiding false reassurance from stable vitals, and dynamically separating stable observation from immediate escalation. This satisfies the Perfect boundary.",
